  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The number of elements in the relation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mo>.</mo></math>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "18",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>}</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>}</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;such that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>}</mo></math></p><p>Now finding discriminant&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>And&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;a perfect square for any possible&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;will be a integer,</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;is a perfect square</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Now for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>{</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>}</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>Total <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> elements belonging to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>And,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is not possible</p><p>Now for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;(not possible)</p><p>Now for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;possible pair will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>{</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>}</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;elements belonging to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math></p><p>Total number of elements will be<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
